WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.180 --> 00:00:02.650
- [Instructor] We are asked,
which problem can we solve

00:00:02.650 --> 00:00:05.890
with 42 divided by seven?

00:00:05.890 --> 00:00:08.930
And they explain three
different scenarios here.

00:00:08.930 --> 00:00:10.010
We need to pick one of them,

00:00:10.010 --> 00:00:12.270
so pause this video and have a go at it

00:00:12.270 --> 00:00:14.020
before we work through it together.

00:00:15.230 --> 00:00:16.830
All right, now let's work
through this together.

00:00:16.830 --> 00:00:17.970
So let's see, choice A says,

00:00:17.970 --> 00:00:21.590
Steven packed 42 candy bars in his bag.

00:00:21.590 --> 00:00:25.670
He gave seven of them away to his friends.

00:00:25.670 --> 00:00:28.640
How many candy bars does Steven have left?

00:00:28.640 --> 00:00:30.250
Well, this isn't a situation of dividing.

00:00:30.250 --> 00:00:32.620
This is a situation
where he starts with 42,

00:00:32.620 --> 00:00:34.540
and he takes seven of them away.

00:00:34.540 --> 00:00:37.610
So this would be the
expression 42 minus seven,

00:00:37.610 --> 00:00:40.640
not the expression 42 divided by seven.

00:00:40.640 --> 00:00:42.010
Rule that one out.

00:00:42.010 --> 00:00:45.040
Julie has seven bags of jellybeans.

00:00:45.040 --> 00:00:48.060
There are 42 jellybeans in one bag.

00:00:48.060 --> 00:00:51.750
How many jellybeans does Julie have?

00:00:51.750 --> 00:00:53.790
Well, for each of those seven bags,

00:00:53.790 --> 00:00:55.760
she has 42 jellybeans.

00:00:55.760 --> 00:01:00.320
So this would be seven times
42, not 42 divided by seven.

00:01:00.320 --> 00:01:01.990
Rule that one out.

00:01:01.990 --> 00:01:05.750
Leslie ran for 42 minutes
total in one week.

00:01:05.750 --> 00:01:08.570
If she ran the same number
of minutes each day,

00:01:08.570 --> 00:01:11.890
how many minutes did
Leslie run in one day?

00:01:11.890 --> 00:01:15.580
So she ran 42 minutes
in total in the week,

00:01:15.580 --> 00:01:17.380
and she ran the same amount every day.

00:01:17.380 --> 00:01:18.670
There's seven days in a week.

00:01:18.670 --> 00:01:21.560
So if we wanna figure out
how much did she run per day,

00:01:21.560 --> 00:01:23.530
you just divide the 42 minutes total

00:01:23.530 --> 00:01:25.650
divided by seven days in a week

00:01:25.650 --> 00:01:27.840
to figure out this would
tell you right over here,

00:01:27.840 --> 00:01:30.750
how many minutes Leslie ran each day.

00:01:30.750 --> 00:01:32.780
And so that is the problem
that we would solve

00:01:32.780 --> 00:01:35.690
with 42 divided by seven.

00:01:35.690 --> 00:01:37.223
Let's do another example.

00:01:38.140 --> 00:01:41.780
Here we are told Kaleb
has 21 action figures.

00:01:41.780 --> 00:01:44.700
He puts three action figures in each box.

00:01:44.700 --> 00:01:48.430
What does the expression 21
divided by three represent?

00:01:48.430 --> 00:01:49.760
So pause this video again,

00:01:49.760 --> 00:01:52.010
and see if you can answer that.

00:01:52.010 --> 00:01:53.300
All right, so this is a situation

00:01:53.300 --> 00:01:55.380
where we're starting with 21,

00:01:55.380 --> 00:01:59.640
and we are dividing it
into groups of three.

00:01:59.640 --> 00:02:04.640
So these are groups, groups of three.

00:02:05.610 --> 00:02:08.860
So this is going to tell
us how many groups we need,

00:02:08.860 --> 00:02:11.860
if we're going to divide
21 into groups of three.

00:02:11.860 --> 00:02:15.830
So if I wrote 21 divided by three,

00:02:15.830 --> 00:02:20.310
and so this is groups of
three, groups of three.

00:02:20.310 --> 00:02:21.890
This is going to be equal to something,

00:02:21.890 --> 00:02:24.020
and many of you might know what this is,

00:02:24.020 --> 00:02:26.840
but this is going to
tell us how many groups,

00:02:26.840 --> 00:02:28.070
how many groups.

00:02:28.070 --> 00:02:30.500
And here a box represents a group.

00:02:30.500 --> 00:02:32.800
How many groups?

00:02:32.800 --> 00:02:36.060
So this is going to be
the number of boxes.

00:02:36.060 --> 00:02:37.900
The number of action figures in each box,

00:02:37.900 --> 00:02:38.733
they already told us.

00:02:38.733 --> 00:02:39.680
There's three in each box,

00:02:39.680 --> 00:02:41.750
so that would be
represented just by a three.

00:02:41.750 --> 00:02:43.050
The total number of action figures,

00:02:43.050 --> 00:02:44.810
that would be 21.

00:02:44.810 --> 00:02:47.250
The number of boxes is the total number

00:02:47.250 --> 00:02:50.490
divided by how many in each box.

00:02:50.490 --> 00:02:51.540
Let's do another one.

00:02:53.300 --> 00:02:58.130
Alex, Brian, and Marta split
a box of 12 cookies evenly.

00:02:58.130 --> 00:03:00.250
Which expression helps us find out

00:03:00.250 --> 00:03:03.790
how many cookies each friend will receive?

00:03:03.790 --> 00:03:06.630
So pause this video again
and see if you can tackle it.

00:03:06.630 --> 00:03:09.000
All right, so we're splitting 12 cookies.

00:03:09.000 --> 00:03:10.190
So we'll start with 12,

00:03:10.190 --> 00:03:11.530
and we need to divide it,

00:03:11.530 --> 00:03:14.460
and how many people are
we dividing it between?

00:03:14.460 --> 00:03:16.870
Well we're dividing it between one, Alex,

00:03:16.870 --> 00:03:20.120
two, Brian, and three people, Marta.

00:03:20.120 --> 00:03:23.530
So we're going to divide
it into three equal groups,

00:03:23.530 --> 00:03:24.930
and you might know what that is,

00:03:24.930 --> 00:03:26.350
but we don't even have to figure that out.

00:03:26.350 --> 00:03:27.600
We just have to say, hey,

00:03:28.610 --> 00:03:31.740
how many cookies does each
of the three people receive?

00:03:31.740 --> 00:03:34.480
Well, it's going to be 12
divided by three cookies.

00:03:34.480 --> 00:03:36.900
So it is this choice right over here.

00:03:36.900 --> 00:03:39.150
Three divided by 12 doesn't
make sense in this situation.

00:03:39.150 --> 00:03:40.150
You don't have three cookies,

00:03:40.150 --> 00:03:42.060
and you're not dividing
it amongst 12 people,

00:03:42.060 --> 00:03:43.470
and C doesn't make sense.

00:03:43.470 --> 00:03:45.140
You're not just taking 12 cookies

00:03:45.140 --> 00:03:46.800
and dividing it between two people.

00:03:46.800 --> 00:03:48.833
You're dividing it between three people.

